# =============================================================
# Signal deployment configuration
# =============================================================
# SOURCE OF TRUTH: AWS SSM Parameter Store (region ap-south-1)
# Fetched at deploy time by scripts/start-docker.sh.
# No secrets live in git, in the deploy bundle, or in this file.
#
# Required parameters (root-level names in the account namespace):
#
#   Name            Type          Purpose
#   DB_USER         String        DB + app datasource username
#   DB_NAME         String        Database name
#   DB_PASSWORD     SecureString  DB password (db init + app datasource)
#   REDIS_PASSWORD  SecureString  Redis requirepass + app client
#   BROKER_APPKEY   SecureString  Broker SSO/XTS app key (endpoint.appKey)
#
# EC2 instance role needs: ssm:GetParameter on these parameter ARNs
# + kms:Decrypt (required for SecureString values).
#
# OPTIONAL local override file on the EC2 host: /opt/signal/.env
#   - not in git, not in the deploy bundle
#   - any variable set there wins over Parameter Store (debug escape hatch)
#
# Normal configuration (not secrets; defaults handled in scripts):
#   IMAGE_TAG       docker image tag (default: latest)
#   ECR_REPO        backend image repo (derived from instance account if unset)
#   FRONTEND_REPO   frontend image repo
#
# Rotation: update the value in Parameter Store, then redeploy.
# Never paste real secret values into this file or any git-tracked file.
